# Company Foundry tools (QC Dono, Batch Genealogy)

Voice-to-text may say “Qsidono”. The SPC app is **QC Dono**. **BATCH GENEALOGY** is a different Foundry tool.

These are internal Palantir Foundry workshops. This public repo must not receive lot numbers, chart images, or other process data.

## QC Dono — authorized use (until the user changes it)

The user authorized **only**:

1. Open **Meeting view** (nothing else).
2. Type into **filter** fields (material number, lot count, etc.).
3. Take screenshots and report what the screen shows (charts, most recent lot).

**Do not:** switch modules/views, click save/submit except as required to apply filters, edit ontology/objects, run pipelines, export beyond on-screen capture, or change data. If a control would write anything besides applying a filter, stop and ask.

If login or the Meeting view is unreachable, report the blocker. Do not guess passwords or probe other Foundry apps.

## BATCH GENEALOGY

Do not open it until the user explicitly asks to try it. Then treat that as its own task.

Playbook: `cloud-notes/playbooks/qc-dono-spc.md`
